; VIRTNET.EXE's description, for cargo drivers: it goes into the zip as
; VIRTNET.INF (with Source= added) and into CATALOG.TXT as one line per
; [Devices] entry. Raise Version= for every change that is published.
; The devices of the kernel's built-in virtio-net driver, which this driver
; replaces (D-231): the transitional device (1000) and the modern-only one
; (1041), both driven through the modern (virtio 1.x) interface.
[Driver]
Name=VIRTNET
Version=1.0.0-1
File=VIRTNET.EXE
Description=virtio network device (virtio 1.x)
Licence=MIT
Basic=Yes

[Devices]
1AF4:1000 network
1AF4:1041 network
